From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Scan out the newest completed XFB copy
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: permanent native VI hardware output transport.

The native VI stopped the game ("Native VI selected XFB output is not
qualified") when a field selected a framebuffer whose newest GX display copy
had not finished on the GPU.

The game reaches that state through its own swap wait. Each frame issues two
draw-done tokens, one after the display copy and one in the swap, and the swap
polls a flag that every draw-done callback sets. On the console the second
token completes right after the first. Natively each token is a GPU
submission on the render worker, so the previous frame's second token can
complete after the current frame's copy token was issued. Its callback then
releases the swap before the copy finishes, and the game flips to that
buffer. Most of these copies still finish before the next retrace; at the
Credits to Options transition they did not.

Keep, per destination, the newest copy whose GPU work completed, recorded
after the existing completion wait, and scan that out. Until a buffer's new
copy completes, the VI shows that buffer's previous completed contents; the
console would scan whatever the copy had written so far. Normal double
buffering is unchanged and nothing waits in the VI interrupt. The draw-done
timing difference itself is unchanged.

diff --git a/lib/gfx/xfb.cpp b/lib/gfx/xfb.cpp
index 520aca3..83b7253 100644
--- a/lib/gfx/xfb.cpp
+++ b/lib/gfx/xfb.cpp
@@ -19,6 +19,9 @@ wgpu::BindGroupLayout g_layout;
 wgpu::RenderPipeline g_pipeline;
 std::mutex g_mutex;
 std::unordered_map<uint32_t, std::shared_ptr<Snapshot>> g_snapshots;
+// Newest copy per destination whose GPU work has completed. A later copy into
+// a buffer the VI is still scanning stays pending until its own completion.
+std::unordered_map<uint32_t, std::shared_ptr<Snapshot>> g_completed;
 uint64_t g_revision = 0;
 
 struct alignas(16) CopyUniforms {
@@ -128,6 +131,9 @@ void complete(const std::shared_ptr<Snapshot>& snapshot) {
   AURORA_ASSERT(webgpu::g_instance.WaitAny(webgpu::g_device.GetLostFuture(), 0) == wgpu::WaitStatus::TimedOut,
       "Original GX XFB completed on a lost device");
   snapshot->gpuComplete.store(true, std::memory_order_release);
+  std::lock_guard lock{g_mutex};
+  auto& completed = g_completed[snapshot->physical];
+  if (!completed || completed->revision < snapshot->revision) completed = snapshot;
 }
 } // namespace
 
@@ -187,6 +193,7 @@ void initialize() {
 
 void shutdown() {
   std::lock_guard lock{g_mutex};
+  g_completed.clear();
   for (const auto& [physical, snapshot] : g_snapshots) {
     AURORA_ASSERT(snapshot.use_count() == 1, "XFB {} still retained during graphics shutdown", physical);
   }
@@ -288,7 +295,7 @@ void encode(const wgpu::CommandEncoder& encoder, wgpu::TextureView source,
 std::shared_ptr<const Snapshot> find(const void* originalDestination) {
   const uint32_t physical = OSCachedToPhysical(const_cast<void*>(originalDestination));
   std::lock_guard lock{g_mutex};
-  const auto it = g_snapshots.find(physical);
-  return it == g_snapshots.end() ? nullptr : it->second;
+  const auto it = g_completed.find(physical);
+  return it == g_completed.end() ? nullptr : it->second;
 }
 } // namespace aurora::gfx::xfb
diff --git a/lib/gfx/xfb.hpp b/lib/gfx/xfb.hpp
index b6262a2..e63140f 100644
--- a/lib/gfx/xfb.hpp
+++ b/lib/gfx/xfb.hpp
@@ -29,7 +29,9 @@ void shutdown();
 void copy_from_bp(uint32_t flags);
 void encode(const wgpu::CommandEncoder& encoder, wgpu::TextureView source,
             Range uniforms, const TextureHandle& destination);
-// The result describes the requested destination, never the latest EFB.
-// Callers must release references before graphics/OS shutdown.
+// The result describes the requested destination, never the latest EFB: the
+// newest copy into it whose GPU work completed (a copy still in flight into a
+// buffer being scanned out does not replace it). Callers must release
+// references before graphics/OS shutdown.
 std::shared_ptr<const Snapshot> find(const void* originalDestination);
 } // namespace aurora::gfx::xfb
